  "//indexes-doc": "Sprint 5 — paginated APIs added in services rely on the indexes below. Firestore auto-creates single-field indexes (e.g. students.fullName ASC, storeProducts.name ASC); only composite indexes need to be declared here. TODO: if `StudentService.getAllPaginated` is invoked with both `status` filter AND ordering by `fullName`, Firestore will need a composite index — declare it on first runtime warning: `students` (status ASC, fullName ASC). Likewise, `StoreService.getProductsPaginated` with `activeOnly: true` will need `storeProducts` (active ASC, name ASC). Both are NOT critical until those flows are wired into UI.",
